WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.632
Navigation jamming and spoofing can endanger aircraft, emergency services, communications,

00:00:04.632 --> 00:00:06.445
transportation, timing, and infrastructure.

00:00:06.445 --> 00:00:11.883
Transmitting interfering or deceptive signals is heavily regulated or prohibited in many

00:00:11.883 --> 00:00:16.415
jurisdictions and can create consequences far beyond one test area.

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:21.400
Do not build, buy, configure, transmit, test, or use jammers, spoofers,

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.120
deceptive signal systems, or interference equipment.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:30.464
Do not attempt to locate a source through unsafe confrontation or unauthorized technical activity.

00:00:30.464 --> 00:00:35.450
When interference is suspected, prioritize safe recovery and immediate operational reporting.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.622
Notify the responsible aviation, safety, compliance, security,

00:00:38.622 --> 00:00:41.794
or operations contact according to organizational procedure.

00:00:41.794 --> 00:00:46.780
Emergency or regulatory channels may apply depending on impact and location.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.858
Preserve original flight logs, controller warnings, media, screenshots, timestamps,

00:00:50.858 --> 00:00:54.484
aircraft and firmware details, weather, route, crew notes,

00:00:54.484 --> 00:00:57.203
and any reports from nearby operations.

00:00:57.203 --> 00:01:01.282
Protect integrity and access, and separate observations from conclusions.

00:01:01.282 --> 00:01:05.814
Coordinate review across aviation safety, technical specialists, compliance, legal, security,

00:01:05.814 --> 00:01:07.174
and affected operations.

00:01:07.174 --> 00:01:11.706
They can determine notification, broader monitoring, equipment inspection, data validity,

00:01:11.706 --> 00:01:14.425
and whether specialized authorities should investigate.

00:01:14.425 --> 00:01:16.691
Responsible reporting avoids sensational attribution.

00:01:16.691 --> 00:01:21.676
State what occurred, what safety action was taken, what evidence exists,

00:01:21.676 --> 00:01:25.755
what remains uncertain, and what operational changes are recommended.

00:01:25.755 --> 00:01:30.740
The objective is risk reduction and learning, not proving an adversary.
